CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17 --pointer-check
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* nothrow new\[\]: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* nothrow new: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* aligned nothrow new\[\]: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* placement new into an array: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] .* placement new\[\] into an array: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
no body for callee
--
The new-placement arguments std::nothrow and std::align_val_t select the
non-throwing and aligned replaceable allocation functions, which allocate
([new.delete.single], [new.delete.array]); they were taken as the address
of the reserved placement form.  An array placement argument decays to a
pointer ([expr.new]/19).
